# VS Code REST Client examples. Set variables locally; do not commit tokens.
@base = http://127.0.0.1:8000/api/v1
@token = {{$processEnv CDRMAPP_LOCAL_TOKEN}}

### Sign in (supply a local password via your process environment)
POST {{base}}/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json
Accept: application/json

{"email":"citizen@synthetic.example.test","password":"{{$processEnv CDRMAPP_LOCAL_PASSWORD}}","device_name":"Local API client"}

### Own or agency-scoped incidents
GET {{base}}/incidents
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Accept: application/json

### Authorized reports needing action (use status=done for completed reports)
GET {{base}}/reports?status=need_action
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Accept: application/json

### Mark an authorized report done; use need_action to mark it undone
PATCH {{base}}/incidents/{{$processEnv CDRMAPP_LOCAL_INCIDENT_ID}}/status
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json
Accept: application/json

{"status":"done"}

### A synthetic report: preserve the exact UUID/payload for retries
POST {{base}}/incidents
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json
Accept: application/json

{"category_id":1,"description":"SYNTHETIC local request example, not a real incident.","latitude":14.5995,"longitude":120.9842,"location_source":"manual","idempotency_key":"205a8472-5b75-4cf4-92d0-dc07b42365de"}

### Authorized aggregate density
GET {{base}}/analytics/heatmap?exploratory=0&west=120&east=122&south=14&north=15
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Accept: application/json
